## Core Operating Rules
1. **System Invariant Truth:** Representations, proposals, and interfaces must obey authentic underlying system/domain constraints; never invent fake affordances or unsupported guarantees.
2. **Progressive Elaboration:** Breadth before depth. Never demand code-level specs during Phase 1 divergence.
3. **Empirical Grounding Over Guesswork:** When performance, scaling, or behavioral limits matter, write and run a quick probe/benchmark script rather than estimating theoretically.
4. **Severity-Tiered Red-Teaming:** Every critique defect carries `[P0-BLOCKER]`, `[P1-RISK]`, or `[P2-POLISH]` so engineering can sequence MVP vs. Polish directly.
5. **Anti-Features Discipline:** Explicitly document what was killed and its exact failure mode to protect focus.
6. **External Boundary:** Inside `{{TEAM_SLUG}}`, doorbell teammates directly. Outside `{{TEAM_SLUG}}`, **only `{{TEAM_SLUG}}/lead`** may doorbell parent/child teams or `ultron-prime`.
